; Program 1 (Part 2 deliverable, source-only for this stage)
; Team integration note:
; - This program is intentionally prepared before full instruction execution is merged.
; - It depends on execution support for IN / OUT / CHK / JZ / JMA.
; - After instruction integration, run and tune behavior as needed.
;
; Behavior goal (current draft):
; 1) Poll keyboard status (device 0)
; 2) Read one word from keyboard (device 0)
; 3) Print that word to printer (device 1)
; 4) Repeat forever
;
; Operand style follows current assembler implementation.

        LOC     16

START:  CHK     1,0         ; R1 <- keyboard ready status (device 0)
        JZ      1,0,START   ; if not ready, keep polling
        IN      0,0         ; R0 <- keyboard input
        OUT     0,1         ; print R0 to printer device
        JMA     1,START     ; loop (assembler currently requires x=1..3 for JMA)
        HLT                 ; safety stop (normally unreachable)
